 Agentic Design Patterns - Google Docs. Every chapter is backed by Google CoLab code and covers the AI coding techniques such as prompt chaining, routing, memory, MCP & multi-agent coordination, guardrails, reasoning, planning",["Agentic Design Patterns Springer Amazon - & - Agentic Design Patterns - Google Docs"]],["Person/Aoife%20O%27Donovan/","source-block-120","Aoife O'Donovan",[]],["Person/Aoife%20O%27Donovan/","source-block-140","About",["Aoife O'Donovan"]],["Person/Aoife%20O%27Donovan/","source-block-152","Singer-songwriter. Wrote \"Show Me\" for Group/Brooklyn Rider/Music/Recording/The Brooklyn Rider Almanac.",["Aoife O'Donovan","About"]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-41","Aram Drevekenin",[]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-90","Open source developer and creator of Zellij, the Rust-based terminal multiplexer",["Aram Drevekenin"]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-182","Also created Bandwhich, a terminal bandwidth utilization tool written in Rust",["Aram Drevekenin"]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-271","Active contributor to the Rust CLI/TUI ecosystem",["Aram Drevekenin"]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-323","Links",["Aram Drevekenin"]],["Person/Aram%20Drevekenin/","source-block-335","GitHub: imsnif",["Aram Drevekenin","Links"]],["Person/Aravind%20Srinivas/","source-block-41","CEO of PerplexityAI",[]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-41","Armin Ronacher",[]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-60","About",["Armin Ronacher"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-72","Python developer and creator of Flask web framework",["Armin Ronacher","About"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-128","Known for work on Werkzeug and other Python libraries",["Armin Ronacher","About"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-186","Author of blog post about agentic coding experiences",["Armin Ronacher","About"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-243","Founder of Earendil (Earendil Works), the company behind PiAI",["Armin Ronacher","About"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-317","Links",["Armin Ronacher"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/","source-block-329","Person/Armin Ronacher/Blog https://lucumr.pocoo.org/2025/6/12/agentic-coding/",["Armin Ronacher","Links"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-94","A Language For Agents - Programming/Language",[]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-207","Metadata",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-222","Author: Person/Armin Ronacher",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Metadata"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-264","Source: lucumr.pocoo.org",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Metadata"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-326","Published: February 09",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Metadata"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-357","Annotated in Readwise: Link",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Metadata"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-457","Key Highlights",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-478","Agents can still perform well in newer or underrepresented languages if documentation and tooling are good enough.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-597","Tooling quality can matter more than language popularity in model weights (example: Swift tooling friction).",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-710","Lower coding cost reduces the importance of ecosystem breadth, because agents can port missing functionality.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-824","A new language can succeed if it is designed with agent behavior and training realities in mind.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-925","As generated code volume increases, readability and reviewability become more important than terseness.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1033","Agents often skip LSP setup, so languages that remain understandable without LSP have an advantage.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1141","Significant whitespace can be a reliability issue for token-level editing workflows.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1230","Structural tokens can also fail when punctuation clusters tokenize poorly.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1309","Agents prefer local reasoning and low-coupling code that avoids hidden context.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1393","Macro-heavy code and alias-heavy imports both degrade agent reliability.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1470","Flaky tests and environment divergence are especially costly for iterative agent workflows.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1566","Unified, deterministic build/test signals help agents converge faster.",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Key Highlights"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-1641","Selected Annotations",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language"]],["Person/Armin%20Ronacher/Blog/26/02/A%20Language%20For%20Agents/","source-block-3313","Note: I haven't had problems with this in months… is this really still a problem?",["A Language For Agents - Programming/Language","Selected Annotations"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-41","Arthur Cecil Pigou",[]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-64","Bio",["Arthur Cecil Pigou"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-74","British economist (1877-1959) associated with welfare economics.",["Arthur Cecil Pigou","Bio"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-143","Best known for work on externalities and corrective taxation.",["Arthur Cecil Pigou","Bio"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-209","The term Pigouvian is named after him.",["Arthur Cecil Pigou","Bio"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-256","Why He Matters",["Arthur Cecil Pigou"]],["Person/Arthur%20Cecil%20Pigou/","source-block-277","Pigou formalized how private incentives can diverge from social costs or benefits.",["Arthur Cecil Pigou","Why He Matters"]]],"format_version":5}